HDSDP — Software for Semidefinite Programming
================================================

HDSDP is a C library and command-line solver for sparse semidefinite programs.
It implements a homogeneous dual-scaling interior-point method. The `sdpasolve`
program reads SDPA `.dat-s` and MPS `.mps` input files. The repository also
contains example instances, a user manual in `doc/`, and the separate ADPCG
and SPEIGS components in `derivative/`.

Project page: https://github.com/COPT-Public/HDSDP
Project manager and contact: Wenzhi Gao <gwz@stanford.edu>

For support, feature requests, and bug reports, open an issue at
https://github.com/COPT-Public/HDSDP/issues. Include the input format, build
platform, the command run, and the relevant solver output when reporting a bug.
The COIN-OR code of conduct is at https://www.coin-or.org/code-of-conduct/.

Requirements and included third-party software
----------------------------------------------

The default build requires CMake 3.21 or later, a C compiler, and BLAS and
LAPACK libraries. On macOS, the system Accelerate framework can provide BLAS
and LAPACK. Optional Pardiso support requires Intel MKL and local configuration
of its library paths; it is disabled by default. See `INSTALL` for the tested
build, install, and run procedure and `TESTING` for the installation test.

The source bundle includes adaptations of SuiteSparse CSparse/CXSparse and LDL
(LGPL-2.1-or-later) and OSQP QDLDL (Apache-2.0). SPEIGS has its own MIT
license. These parts retain their own licenses; the top-level `LICENSE` records
the project's MIT notice. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES` and the
license files under `external/lics/` and `derivative/SPEIGS/`.

Quick start
-----------

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    cmake --build build --parallel
    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
    cmake --install build --prefix "$PWD/install"
    ./install/bin/sdpasolve examples/truss1.dat-s

The example should report `SDP Status: Primal dual optimal`. For the solver
API and other examples, see `doc/hdsdp_doc.pdf` and `interface/hdsdp.h`.

Research reference
------------------

Wenzhi Gao, Dongdong Ge, and Yinyu Ye, “HDSDP: Software for Semidefinite
Programming,” arXiv:2207.13862 (2022).
